==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪz.əl/|/ˈmɪz.l̩/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪzəl|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|misellen||to drizzle}}. Cognate with {{cog|nds|musseln||to mizzle}}, {{cog|nl|miezelen||to drizzle, rain gently}}. Of obscure origin, but apparently related to {{etyl|gml|-}} {{m|de|mes||urine}}, {{cog|dum|mes}}, {{m|dum|mis||urine}}, both from {{cog|osx|mehs||urine}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*mihstuz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mihstaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mihsk-||urine}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*mīganą||to urinate}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*meiǵʰ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*omeiǵʰ-||to urinate}}. Compare also {{cog|en|micturate||to urinate}}, {{cog|ofs|mese||urine}}, {{cog|nds|miegen||to urinate}}, {{cog|nl|mijgen||to urinate}}, {{cog|da|mige||to urinate}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|mizzl}}

# {{label|en|intransitive|now|_|regional|UK|North America}} To [[rain]] in very fine drops.

